Tier-2: the three silent ways a SPARTA deck ends up at the wrong density.

  * create_particles n <N>0> ignores global nrho and makes exactly N;
  * a nrho keyword on the MIXTURE overrides global nrho;
  * global nrho/fnum issued after create_particles is too late -> 0 particles;
  * a region argument scales the requested count by the volume fraction and
    suppresses SPARTA's own 'Created unexpected # of particles' warning.

All four exit 0 with no warning. COVERS (added 2026-08-06): the two universal density-override claims. The 'global after create_particles' case this script also runs belongs to universal:0, which is attributed to global_nrho_before_create_particles, where the full Signal (Np zero on every stats line, no warning) is executed. POSITIONAL ALIASES added 2026-08-06: this fixture's universal claims are also listed at their slots in the rarefied_flow row. The identity key 'universal:<n>' counts each shared claim once, which is correct; but an external counter walking rarefied_flow's 19 positional slots cannot see it and reports the claim as uncovered. Listing both makes the coverage visible under either convention; the gate collapses the alias onto the identity key so it is still counted once. MUTATION CONTROL (added 2026-08-06, re-runnable): T2_MUTATE=1 writes each of the four wrong decks the way the documentation prescribes, one token per deck and nothing else — 'n 500' becomes 'n 0', the 'nrho 1e21' keyword comes off the mixture line, the global nrho/fnum line moves back in front of create_particles, and the 'region half' restriction comes off. Every deck then lands on the density global nrho asks for: created_n500 goes 500 -> 999, created_mixture_nrho_1e21 goes 14 -> 999, created_global_after goes 0 -> 999 and created_n500_in_half_region goes 250 -> 500. Verified: unmutated the fixture PASSES (rc=0); with T2_MUTATE=1 it FAILS (rc=1) and these expect_in_output strings go False and disappear: n_nonzero_overrides_nrho=True, mixture_nrho_overrides_global=True, global_after_create_particles_gives_zero=True, region_scales_the_requested_count=True. Re-verify: cd scripts/tier2_fixtures/sparta/create_particles_and_mixture_nrho_overrides && python source.py (passes, rc=0), then T2_MUTATE=1 python source.py (fails, rc=1). Needs a SPARTA binary: the fixtures find spa_serial/spa_mpi on PATH or at ~/Schreibtisch/sparta/src/spa_serial, else set SPARTA_BINARY; with none present they exit 0 on a SKIP: line. POSITIONAL ALIAS REPOINTED 2026-08-07: eight new rarefied_flow claims were inserted ahead of the shared universal block, moving it from slots 9-18 to 17-26. This fixture's rarefied_flow:<n> entries are the positional spelling of the universal:<n> claims it already names by identity, so only the alias number changed; the evidence, the decks and the mutation control are untouched. The runner key moved with it: pitfall_index 10 -> 18, so this fixture still writes its own row in tier2_results.json.
